verdict.recommended_fix:
Before running `r4_seal.py --seal`, add one paragraph to PROTOCOL.md §0 or §7. It should say that, before the first outer score of any S-slot, a single stage-1 amendment seals:
(a) the finalist-selection rule: statistic, design (BP/BPG handling) and tie-break;
(b) numeric stage gates, including the inner-fold-only signal over B1/B2 and the coverage threshold required before encoder training (S07/S10);
(c) the route rules for S09 and S19, using inner-only evidence or already-labelled dev results;
(d) the confirmatory family and the multiplicity rule.

The paragraph should also say that all arms and controls of a stage block are sealed together in one amendment before any of them is scored. The blocks are S01–S04 + S21; S05–S10 + S22/S23; and S11–S16 + S24. It should state that this amendment lists the B1/B2 dev results (pooled, per pair and per subgroup) as seen.

Finally, fill in data_version for S14–S16 and S24 in EXPERIMENT_REGISTRY.csv, for example "V1 + matched auxiliary (as S13)". Nothing else in the stage-0 seal has to change.

